1
00:00:00,250 --> 00:00:04,066
We have time for dinner at the neighborhood
restaurant.

2
00:00:04,216 --> 00:00:06,784
Everyone can choose something they enjoy.

3
00:00:06,934 --> 00:00:09,919
I will be our extremely prepared diner.

4
00:00:10,069 --> 00:00:14,300
Will you be prepared to let us order for
ourselves?

5
00:00:15,250 --> 00:00:17,970
Can we look at a menu?

6
00:00:18,120 --> 00:00:20,840
Will there be room for six?

7
00:00:20,990 --> 00:00:24,150
We will ask for a table together.

8
00:00:24,300 --> 00:00:28,780
I want a seat where I can hear everybody
order.

9
00:00:30,250 --> 00:00:33,410
Esteemed keeper of dinner, we humbly request—

10
00:00:33,560 --> 00:00:35,840
A simple question will work.

11
00:00:35,990 --> 00:00:38,710
I may have overdressed the sentence.

12
00:00:38,860 --> 00:00:42,900
Try that sentence in your regular dinner
voice, Dan.

13
00:00:45,250 --> 00:00:47,530
Will everything be too hot?

14
00:00:47,680 --> 00:00:52,600
We can ask, and let food cool when it needs
to.

15
00:00:52,750 --> 00:00:55,030
Clear questions. I am ready.

16
00:00:55,180 --> 00:00:59,220
I want to know before my tongue finds out.

17
00:01:00,250 --> 00:01:03,757
Eighty dollars for the meal, tax, and tip.

18
00:01:03,907 --> 00:01:06,986
We will check the prices before ordering.

19
00:01:07,136 --> 00:01:09,786
A budget that includes the ending.

20
00:01:09,936 --> 00:01:14,300
That's my favorite part to know before we sit
down.

21
00:01:15,250 --> 00:01:18,410
Perhaps a dessert taller than this kitchen—

22
00:01:18,560 --> 00:01:21,720
We have not seen the menu yet.

23
00:01:21,870 --> 00:01:24,150
Let us start with dinner.

24
00:01:24,300 --> 00:01:29,220
Fair. My eyes can order all the imaginary
dessert they like.

25
00:01:30,250 --> 00:01:32,090
I can check prices.

26
00:01:32,240 --> 00:01:35,400
I want to choose my own dinner.

27
00:01:35,550 --> 00:01:39,150
Of course. Max can ask for water too.

28
00:01:39,300 --> 00:01:43,780
I know that one already. Can I try it there?

29
00:01:45,250 --> 00:01:47,702
I have shortened my speech.

30
00:01:47,852 --> 00:01:48,884
How short?

31
00:01:49,034 --> 00:01:53,379
Good evening. That should get us through the
door.

32
00:01:53,529 --> 00:01:57,400
Let's see if dinner fits through with you.

33
00:02:00,250 --> 00:02:01,326
Good evening.

34
00:02:01,476 --> 00:02:04,031
That was an excellent length.

35
00:02:04,181 --> 00:02:07,722
We all fit through the door too.

36
00:02:07,872 --> 00:02:12,400
So far, nobody's needed a dictionary to
understand Dad.

37
00:02:15,250 --> 00:02:18,850
Could we have a table for six, please?

38
00:02:19,000 --> 00:02:22,600
Certainly. The table by the window is ready.

39
00:02:22,750 --> 00:02:23,710
Thank you.

40
00:02:23,860 --> 00:02:28,340
The window sounds good. We'll all be able to
see.

41
00:02:30,250 --> 00:02:33,850
Stay beside me. This aisle is for everyone.

42
00:02:34,000 --> 00:02:36,720
I will wait for Leo's chair.

43
00:02:36,870 --> 00:02:38,710
No chair traffic jam.

44
00:02:38,860 --> 00:02:43,340
I'll tuck in here. Ella, there's room for you
now.

45
00:02:45,250 --> 00:02:47,090
Three on this side.

46
00:02:47,240 --> 00:02:49,520
Three on the window side.

47
00:02:49,670 --> 00:02:53,710
A table with exactly the right audience for
dinner.

48
00:02:53,860 --> 00:02:57,900
Good. We can hear one another from both sides.

49
00:03:00,250 --> 00:03:03,791
Here are your menus. Take your time.

50
00:03:03,941 --> 00:03:05,017
Thank you.

51
00:03:05,167 --> 00:03:07,229
We will choose together.

52
00:03:07,379 --> 00:03:12,400
I'll start with the part that actually looks
like dinner.

53
00:03:15,250 --> 00:03:18,850
Do I have to read the whole book?

54
00:03:19,000 --> 00:03:22,160
Only the parts that help you choose.

55
00:03:22,310 --> 00:03:25,030
The dinner section is right here.

56
00:03:25,180 --> 00:03:29,220
A book where I get to choose the ending!

57
00:03:30,250 --> 00:03:32,530
Could we have water, please?

58
00:03:32,680 --> 00:03:35,400
Of course. Six glasses of water.

59
00:03:35,550 --> 00:03:39,150
My speech has been defeated by six words.

60
00:03:39,300 --> 00:03:43,340
Good. My mouth was dry just listening to
yours.

61
00:03:45,250 --> 00:03:48,175
Your water. There is no charge.

62
00:03:48,325 --> 00:03:49,357
Thank you.

63
00:03:49,507 --> 00:03:52,906
Mine has its own safe parking place.

64
00:03:53,056 --> 00:03:57,400
Leave it there, Max. There's room beside your
menu.

65
00:04:00,250 --> 00:04:02,090
Appetizers, main courses, desserts.

66
00:04:02,240 --> 00:04:05,400
I am ready for a main course.

67
00:04:05,550 --> 00:04:09,590
Then our dinner can begin in the middle
section.

68
00:04:09,740 --> 00:04:13,780
Great. I don't think my stomach wants an
introduction.

69
00:04:15,250 --> 00:04:18,410
The vegetable pasta sounds good. Twelve
dollars.

70
00:04:18,560 --> 00:04:20,840
With the vegetables listed here?

71
00:04:20,990 --> 00:04:24,150
Yes. That is the one I want.

72
00:04:24,300 --> 00:04:28,340
I can see why you picked that one, Maya.

73
00:04:30,250 --> 00:04:32,970
Grilled chicken with rice for me.

74
00:04:33,120 --> 00:04:36,280
One main course, with the rice included?

75
00:04:36,430 --> 00:04:38,270
Exactly. Fourteen dollars together.

76
00:04:38,420 --> 00:04:42,460
Good. I was about to count the rice twice.

77
00:04:45,250 --> 00:04:47,900
I would like the cheese sandwich.

78
00:04:48,050 --> 00:04:50,700
You can tell the server yourself.

79
00:04:50,850 --> 00:04:54,786
Eight dollars. I have its place in our plan.

80
00:04:54,936 --> 00:04:59,300
I'd like to do the asking for my own sandwich.

81
00:05:00,250 --> 00:05:03,410
Does the baked potato include the vegetables?

82
00:05:03,560 --> 00:05:05,840
Yes. The filling is included.

83
00:05:05,990 --> 00:05:08,710
Then I would like that, please.

84
00:05:08,860 --> 00:05:13,780
Good question, Ella. Now you know exactly what
comes with it.

85
00:05:15,250 --> 00:05:18,234
There is a smaller chicken and rice.

86
00:05:18,384 --> 00:05:20,538
That can be your dinner.

87
00:05:20,688 --> 00:05:24,919
That one, please. I like a plate made for me.

88
00:05:25,069 --> 00:05:29,300
We can spot yours next to Nina's when it
comes.

89
00:05:30,250 --> 00:05:33,410
The tomato soup looks right for me.

90
00:05:33,560 --> 00:05:36,720
What kind of flavor would you enjoy?

91
00:05:36,870 --> 00:05:38,710
Something comforting. And hot.

92
00:05:38,860 --> 00:05:42,900
Hot like a pepper, or hot like the pan?

93
00:05:45,250 --> 00:05:48,329
I would like the soup hot, please.

94
00:05:48,479 --> 00:05:52,414
Do you mean its temperature, or a spicy
flavor?

95
00:05:52,564 --> 00:05:55,214
Those are different kinds of hot?

96
00:05:55,364 --> 00:05:59,300
Listen to the question, Dan. Which did you
mean?

97
00:06:00,250 --> 00:06:02,152
This pepper means spicy.

98
00:06:02,302 --> 00:06:05,113
I was thinking of warm soup.

99
00:06:05,263 --> 00:06:08,529
Then we should say both things clearly.

100
00:06:08,679 --> 00:06:12,400
Right. My tongue had one temperature in mind.

101
00:06:15,250 --> 00:06:17,970
Should I rescue Dad with water?

102
00:06:18,120 --> 00:06:19,960
Nothing spicy has arrived.

103
00:06:20,110 --> 00:06:24,150
I need a better sentence, not a rescue team.

104
00:06:24,300 --> 00:06:28,340
I'll save my water for drinking with my
dinner.

105
00:06:30,250 --> 00:06:33,410
Mild tomato soup, please. Warm, not extra-hot.

106
00:06:33,560 --> 00:06:35,400
Certainly. No chili added.

107
00:06:35,550 --> 00:06:38,710
That tells us exactly what you want.

108
00:06:38,860 --> 00:06:43,340
Yes. That sounds like the soup I came here
for.

109
00:06:45,250 --> 00:06:49,186
Could we change the note before you send it?

110
00:06:49,336 --> 00:06:52,843
Of course. It now says mild and warm.

111
00:06:52,993 --> 00:06:55,214
No guessing reaches the kitchen.

112
00:06:55,364 --> 00:06:59,300
That's one note I'm glad we checked in time.

113
00:07:00,250 --> 00:07:02,819
One meal for each of us.

114
00:07:02,969 --> 00:07:06,784
My chicken plate and Max's smaller plate are
separate.

115
00:07:06,934 --> 00:07:10,334
And my soup is dinner, not an appetizer.

116
00:07:10,484 --> 00:07:14,300
Six mains, then. Let's see how that adds up.

117
00:07:15,250 --> 00:07:17,970
Fifty-eight dollars for the six meals.

118
00:07:18,120 --> 00:07:19,960
Before tax and tip.

119
00:07:20,110 --> 00:07:24,590
Then the calculator has one more part of the
story.

120
00:07:24,740 --> 00:07:28,780
Let's get that part right before the check
comes.

121
00:07:30,250 --> 00:07:33,329
This menu lists ten percent sales tax.

122
00:07:33,479 --> 00:07:35,700
That adds five dollars eighty.

123
00:07:35,850 --> 00:07:39,786
Sixty-three eighty before our tip. Still room
to plan.

124
00:07:39,936 --> 00:07:44,300
Good. The tip still needs its own place in
there.

125
00:07:45,250 --> 00:07:47,970
Let us plan a ten-dollar tip.

126
00:07:48,120 --> 00:07:49,960
That fits our budget.

127
00:07:50,110 --> 00:07:53,710
Seventy-three eighty altogether. Six twenty
stays with us.

128
00:07:53,860 --> 00:07:58,340
Good. We can enjoy dinner without guessing at
the end.

129
00:08:00,250 --> 00:08:01,697
Cheese sandwich, please.

130
00:08:01,847 --> 00:08:04,658
The baked potato with its vegetables.

131
00:08:04,808 --> 00:08:07,620
The children's chicken and rice, please.

132
00:08:07,770 --> 00:08:12,400
Good thing we each got to say our own part.

133
00:08:15,250 --> 00:08:17,530
Vegetable pasta for me, please.

134
00:08:17,680 --> 00:08:19,960
The adult chicken and rice.

135
00:08:20,110 --> 00:08:24,150
Mild tomato soup, warm rather than extra-hot.
Thank you.

136
00:08:24,300 --> 00:08:28,780
That's all three of us. Thanks for checking
the soup.

137
00:08:30,250 --> 00:08:32,970
Any ingredient restrictions I should flag?

138
00:08:33,120 --> 00:08:36,720
We checked the listed ingredients for our
family.

139
00:08:36,870 --> 00:08:40,030
No changes to this order, thank you.

140
00:08:40,180 --> 00:08:43,780
Just the soup the way we agreed, please.

141
00:08:45,250 --> 00:08:49,730
Six mains, including the mild, warm soup.
Sending it now.

142
00:08:49,880 --> 00:08:53,480
Thank you. That was easier than my speech.

143
00:08:53,630 --> 00:08:56,790
Did the kitchen get the corrected note?

144
00:08:56,940 --> 00:08:59,220
Yes, exactly as you asked.

145
00:09:00,250 --> 00:09:04,066
Does dinner need a quiet minute like pancake
batter?

146
00:09:04,216 --> 00:09:06,369
It needs time to cook.

147
00:09:06,519 --> 00:09:09,503
We are getting good at that part.

148
00:09:09,653 --> 00:09:14,300
Good. I think my fork is less patient than the
batter.

149
00:09:15,250 --> 00:09:17,970
And now, the very patient fork.

150
00:09:18,120 --> 00:09:21,720
It has nothing to say until dinner arrives.

151
00:09:21,870 --> 00:09:23,710
A beautifully quiet introduction.

152
00:09:23,860 --> 00:09:27,900
Listen. It's doing a very good job of waiting.

153
00:09:30,250 --> 00:09:33,234
Can mild food still be too hot?

154
00:09:33,384 --> 00:09:36,369
Yes. Mild describes flavor. Temperature is
different.

155
00:09:36,519 --> 00:09:39,919
That was the missing half of my sentence.

156
00:09:40,069 --> 00:09:44,300
So I'll still give mine a minute if it steams.

157
00:09:45,250 --> 00:09:49,290
I guessed a whole breakfast from one word
once.

158
00:09:49,440 --> 00:09:51,280
Context helped then too.

159
00:09:51,430 --> 00:09:55,030
This time you asked before anything went
wrong.

160
00:09:55,180 --> 00:09:59,220
One little question is cheaper than another
whole dinner.

161
00:10:00,250 --> 00:10:02,900
Are we missing the appetizer part?

162
00:10:03,050 --> 00:10:05,271
We chose dinner without one.

163
00:10:05,421 --> 00:10:09,786
The menu is a choice, not a list to finish.

164
00:10:09,936 --> 00:10:14,300
Good. My smaller plate is a whole dinner for
me.

165
00:10:15,250 --> 00:10:18,410
I prepared a request for more water.

166
00:10:18,560 --> 00:10:20,840
Your glass still has plenty.

167
00:10:20,990 --> 00:10:24,590
Then my request can wait beside my speech.

168
00:10:24,740 --> 00:10:28,780
Your glass appreciates a little peace and
quiet too.

169
00:10:30,250 --> 00:10:33,410
Let us leave room for the server.

170
00:10:33,560 --> 00:10:35,840
My hands can wait here.

171
00:10:35,990 --> 00:10:39,150
Mine too. Dinner gets a clear landing.

172
00:10:39,300 --> 00:10:43,780
I'll keep my elbows in. There's room on this
side.

173
00:10:45,250 --> 00:10:48,850
Vegetable pasta, and the adult chicken and
rice.

174
00:10:49,000 --> 00:10:51,280
That is mine, thank you.

175
00:10:51,430 --> 00:10:53,710
And this one is mine.

176
00:10:53,860 --> 00:10:57,900
That chicken looks like the size Nina asked
for.

177
00:11:00,250 --> 00:11:01,650
My cheese sandwich.

178
00:11:01,800 --> 00:11:04,960
And the baked potato I asked about.

179
00:11:05,110 --> 00:11:09,590
Keep the hot plate on the table while it
cools.

180
00:11:09,740 --> 00:11:13,780
The middle still looks steamy. I'll give it
time.

181
00:11:15,250 --> 00:11:19,290
Mild tomato soup, and the children's chicken
and rice.

182
00:11:19,440 --> 00:11:20,400
Thank you.

183
00:11:20,550 --> 00:11:24,150
We will check the temperature before we begin.

184
00:11:24,300 --> 00:11:28,340
I see mine. The chicken's on the smaller
plate.

185
00:11:30,250 --> 00:11:32,530
Six orders, six correct dinners.

186
00:11:32,680 --> 00:11:34,960
Mine has the vegetables included.

187
00:11:35,110 --> 00:11:39,150
And mine has a smaller plate, just as
promised.

188
00:11:39,300 --> 00:11:43,340
And nobody had to send a single dinner back.

189
00:11:45,250 --> 00:11:47,900
I will check a little first.

190
00:11:48,050 --> 00:11:51,986
And we let it cool if it needs to.

191
00:11:52,136 --> 00:11:54,786
Even when the flavor is mild.

192
00:11:54,936 --> 00:11:59,300
Good point. Those are two different checks for
my soup.

193
00:12:00,250 --> 00:12:02,530
Is that what you wanted?

194
00:12:02,680 --> 00:12:04,960
Yes. Mild flavor, comfortably warm.

195
00:12:05,110 --> 00:12:09,150
A much better description than one very busy
word.

196
00:12:09,300 --> 00:12:13,780
A word can have a very tiring day at dinner.

197
00:12:15,250 --> 00:12:17,530
The middle needs another moment.

198
00:12:17,680 --> 00:12:19,080
You can wait.

199
00:12:19,230 --> 00:12:23,270
Dinner is not a race to the hottest bite.

200
00:12:23,420 --> 00:12:27,900
Then the center of my potato can take its
time.

201
00:12:30,250 --> 00:12:32,090
How is your dinner?

202
00:12:32,240 --> 00:12:36,280
Good. My napkin has more work than your
speech.

203
00:12:36,430 --> 00:12:39,590
It came prepared for the right job.

204
00:12:39,740 --> 00:12:43,780
I bet my napkin never rehearsed a single word.

205
00:12:45,250 --> 00:12:47,970
I liked saying my own order.

206
00:12:48,120 --> 00:12:50,400
You knew what you wanted.

207
00:12:50,550 --> 00:12:54,150
And I liked asking what came with mine.

208
00:12:54,300 --> 00:12:58,780
It's nice when the person taking the order
hears you.

209
00:13:00,250 --> 00:13:03,850
The server saved my dinner with one question.

210
00:13:04,000 --> 00:13:06,720
They gave you room to explain.

211
00:13:06,870 --> 00:13:10,030
And you used it. That worked well.

212
00:13:10,180 --> 00:13:14,220
I'd have got something very different without
that question.

213
00:13:15,250 --> 00:13:18,410
Will we ever hear your big speech?

214
00:13:18,560 --> 00:13:22,600
It is enjoying a quiet dinner in my pocket.

215
00:13:22,750 --> 00:13:24,590
A very well-behaved speech.

216
00:13:24,740 --> 00:13:28,340
Good. It can listen while we finish ours.

217
00:13:30,250 --> 00:13:33,410
The library is open tomorrow, isn't it?

218
00:13:33,560 --> 00:13:36,280
We can check the hours later.

219
00:13:36,430 --> 00:13:39,150
Tonight we can finish dinner together.

220
00:13:39,300 --> 00:13:43,340
Deal. The books will still be there after
dinner.

221
00:13:45,250 --> 00:13:47,530
No rescue needed after all.

222
00:13:47,680 --> 00:13:49,960
Just a drink with dinner.

223
00:13:50,110 --> 00:13:53,710
And a safe place to put it back.

224
00:13:53,860 --> 00:13:58,340
Right beside my plate, where my elbow can miss
it.

225
00:14:00,250 --> 00:14:02,819
We can take a comfortable pause.

226
00:14:02,969 --> 00:14:06,784
I would like to save the rest of mine.

227
00:14:06,934 --> 00:14:10,334
Then we can ask for a takeout box.

228
00:14:10,484 --> 00:14:14,300
Saving a little sounds better than eating past
full.

229
00:14:15,250 --> 00:14:18,410
Could we have one takeout box, please?

230
00:14:18,560 --> 00:14:19,410
Certainly.

231
00:14:19,560 --> 00:14:24,040
For the rest of Max's dinner, not a second
dinner.

232
00:14:24,190 --> 00:14:28,230
Good. I'd like my own dinner again another
day.

233
00:14:30,250 --> 00:14:31,756
Here you are.

234
00:14:31,906 --> 00:14:32,938
Thank you.

235
00:14:33,088 --> 00:14:37,432
An empty box waiting for food we already have.

236
00:14:37,582 --> 00:14:42,400
I'll hold it right beside your plate while we
pack.

237
00:14:45,250 --> 00:14:47,970
Your remaining dinner goes in once.

238
00:14:48,120 --> 00:14:50,840
So my plate is empty now.

239
00:14:50,990 --> 00:14:54,590
And the box has the part you saved.

240
00:14:54,740 --> 00:14:58,780
Exactly. You'll be able to recognize your own
supper.

241
00:15:00,250 --> 00:15:04,290
We will go straight home and refrigerate this
promptly.

242
00:15:04,440 --> 00:15:05,840
No extra stops.

243
00:15:05,990 --> 00:15:09,150
My dinner has a sensible travel plan.

244
00:15:09,300 --> 00:15:13,780
And it'll have somebody beside it all the way
home.

245
00:15:15,250 --> 00:15:16,697
I am finished.

246
00:15:16,847 --> 00:15:17,839
Me too.

247
00:15:17,989 --> 00:15:23,074
Then we can ask for the check when everyone is
ready.

248
00:15:23,224 --> 00:15:27,400
I'm ready. My fork can take the evening off.

249
00:15:30,250 --> 00:15:33,850
My imaginary tall dessert can stay imaginary
tonight.

250
00:15:34,000 --> 00:15:35,840
I am satisfied too.

251
00:15:35,990 --> 00:15:39,590
Then our order is complete as it is.

252
00:15:39,740 --> 00:15:43,780
My imaginary dessert didn't cost the budget a
cent.

253
00:15:45,250 --> 00:15:48,175
Could we have the check, please?

254
00:15:48,325 --> 00:15:51,723
Of course. I will bring it over.

255
00:15:51,873 --> 00:15:52,906
Thank you.

256
00:15:53,056 --> 00:15:57,400
Let's look it over together when it gets here.

257
00:16:00,250 --> 00:16:02,970
This box is coming with us.

258
00:16:03,120 --> 00:16:06,280
Of course. I will leave it here.

259
00:16:06,430 --> 00:16:08,710
It has its own traveler.

260
00:16:08,860 --> 00:16:12,900
Yes, the little chicken dinner is traveling
with me.

261
00:16:15,250 --> 00:16:17,090
Here is your check.

262
00:16:17,240 --> 00:16:18,200
Thank you.

263
00:16:18,350 --> 00:16:21,070
May I help check the numbers?

264
00:16:21,220 --> 00:16:25,260
Please do. Start by counting the dinners we
ordered.

265
00:16:25,410 --> 00:16:29,010
I'll start at the top of the check.

266
00:16:30,250 --> 00:16:33,850
Six meals. No extra soup, starter, or dessert.

267
00:16:34,000 --> 00:16:35,840
And water is free.

268
00:16:35,990 --> 00:16:40,030
The order on paper matches the dinner we had.

269
00:16:40,180 --> 00:16:44,220
Good. Now let's check what happens after the
subtotal.

270
00:16:45,250 --> 00:16:47,229
Fifty-eight plus five eighty.

271
00:16:47,379 --> 00:16:48,411
Sixty-three eighty.

272
00:16:48,561 --> 00:16:53,379
Our planned tip is separate. Good to check
before paying.

273
00:16:53,529 --> 00:16:57,400
Right. We can still see both amounts
separately.

274
00:17:00,250 --> 00:17:03,850
Shall we keep the ten-dollar tip we planned?

275
00:17:04,000 --> 00:17:04,850
Yes.

276
00:17:05,000 --> 00:17:08,600
Seventy-three eighty altogether. Still inside
our eighty-dollar plan.

277
00:17:08,750 --> 00:17:13,670
Good. I want to thank them for asking about
the soup.

278
00:17:15,250 --> 00:17:17,530
Does your speech pay too?

279
00:17:17,680 --> 00:17:20,840
No. Just the money in this wallet.

280
00:17:20,990 --> 00:17:23,710
Then the speech can keep resting.

281
00:17:23,860 --> 00:17:27,900
It hasn't earned a tip for all that talking.

282
00:17:30,250 --> 00:17:33,850
Do I pay here or at the counter?

283
00:17:34,000 --> 00:17:36,280
At the service counter, please.

284
00:17:36,430 --> 00:17:39,590
We will wait here with the children.

285
00:17:39,740 --> 00:17:44,220
I'll take the check over. You keep the box
here.

286
00:17:45,250 --> 00:17:47,530
I will be right back.

287
00:17:47,680 --> 00:17:49,520
We will be here.

288
00:17:49,670 --> 00:17:53,270
And our takeout traveler is staying with me.

289
00:17:53,420 --> 00:17:57,460
Good. We'll have everything together when you
come back.

290
00:18:00,250 --> 00:18:01,650
Eighty dollars, please.

291
00:18:01,800 --> 00:18:06,280
Thank you. Your change is sixteen dollars and
twenty cents.

292
00:18:06,430 --> 00:18:09,590
So that's the change before my tip?

293
00:18:09,740 --> 00:18:12,900
Yes. The check itself was sixty-three eighty.

294
00:18:15,250 --> 00:18:18,410
Sixteen twenty in change, before the tip.

295
00:18:18,560 --> 00:18:19,520
That's right.

296
00:18:19,670 --> 00:18:20,630
Thank you.

297
00:18:20,780 --> 00:18:25,700
You can count it here before you put the rest
away.

298
00:18:25,850 --> 00:18:28,570
Good. I'll keep the tip separate.

299
00:18:30,250 --> 00:18:35,021
This ten dollars is a tip. Thank you for
checking my order.

300
00:18:35,171 --> 00:18:37,592
Thank you. Have a lovely evening.

301
00:18:37,742 --> 00:18:40,554
It made a difference to my dinner.

302
00:18:40,704 --> 00:18:44,300
I'm glad the soup came the way you wanted.

303
00:18:45,250 --> 00:18:48,850
Receipt, remaining change, and a much smaller
speech.

304
00:18:49,000 --> 00:18:51,720
All set. Thank you for coming.

305
00:18:51,870 --> 00:18:55,030
Six twenty left after the tip, then?

306
00:18:55,180 --> 00:18:58,340
Exactly. That's your receipt to take home.

307
00:19:00,250 --> 00:19:01,282
Everyone ready?

308
00:19:01,432 --> 00:19:03,884
One box, all our people.

309
00:19:04,034 --> 00:19:07,432
And no speech left on the table.

310
00:19:07,582 --> 00:19:12,400
Good. The little chicken dinner is coming home
with us.

311
00:19:15,250 --> 00:19:17,530
What stayed in the budget?

312
00:19:17,680 --> 00:19:20,400
Six twenty after the ten-dollar tip.

313
00:19:20,550 --> 00:19:24,590
Seventy-three eighty spent. The numbers reach
the same ending.

314
00:19:24,740 --> 00:19:29,220
Good thing we counted from the eighty we
actually brought.

315
00:19:30,250 --> 00:19:33,410
What will your next big speech be?

316
00:19:33,560 --> 00:19:36,280
Could I have some water, please?

317
00:19:36,430 --> 00:19:39,590
Perfect. Now straight home with our box.

318
00:19:39,740 --> 00:19:43,780
Good. At least the box doesn't need a menu.

319
00:19:45,250 --> 00:19:48,850
A warm dinner and a very clear evening.

320
00:19:49,000 --> 00:19:50,400
Good questions helped.

321
00:19:50,550 --> 00:19:53,710
And nobody had to eat a speech.

322
00:19:53,860 --> 00:19:58,780
I liked that we each got to choose our own
dinner.
